1. Mesa (Turnip / freedreno Vulkan driver)
   ----------------------------------------
   The bundled native library `libvulkan_freedreno.so` (located in
   app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/) is a compiled build of the Mesa
   freedreno (Turnip) Vulkan driver, Mesa 26.3.0-devel (git-9c475fc367),
   reporting Vulkan 1.4.335.

   The prebuilt binary was obtained from the
   whitebelyash/AdrenoToolsDrivers repository (release tu_v31,
   "mainline-turnip-sync-V31"). The author describes it as
   "Upstream Turnip driver with some hacks, built from the turnip/gen8
   branch." It is therefore a modified build, NOT a verbatim build of
   upstream Mesa main; the modifications are authored by whitebelyash
   and are not part of the official Mesa source tree.

   The DT_SONAME has been patched from "libvulkan_freedreno.so" to
   "vulkan.adreno.so" following the convention used by official FCL
   Turnip driver plugins. FCL loads the driver by the hardcoded file
   name "libvulkan_freedreno.so" (via driver_helper.c linker_ns_dlopen)
   and its linkerhook intercepts any dlopen request whose file name
   contains "vulkan." to return this driver handle; the SONAME value
   itself does not drive the substitution but is kept consistent with
   the upstream plugin convention. Only the SONAME string in the ELF
   .dynstr table was modified (zero-padded); no code or other data was
   changed. The patch is reproducible via tools/patch_soname.py.

